     which means that if a regular expression matches another defined mount point,
     it will override the previously defined threshold.
 
+    A mount that is normally busy but suddenly shows very low usage is often a
+    sign that the filesystem failed to mount, leaving the mount point as an
+    empty directory on the root filesystem. To catch this, specify a mapping
+    with ``min`` and/or ``max`` keys instead of a bare percentage. ``max``
+    behaves exactly like the plain percentage form above; ``min`` triggers the
+    beacon when usage falls to or below the given percentage.
+
+    .. code-block:: yaml
+
+        beacons:
+          diskusage:
+            - /mnt/nfs:
+                min: 20%
+                max: 90%
+
+    ``min`` and ``max`` may also be used independently of one another.
+
     """
     whitelist = []
     config = salt.utils.beacons.remove_hidden_options(config, whitelist)
@@ -106,6 +123,14 @@ def beacon(config):
